# Review is requested automatically on the paths where a well-meaning change is
# most likely to break something the diff does not show.
#
# THIS IS NOT A GENERAL REVIEW REQUIREMENT, and that is deliberate. The default
# branch requires no approving review: an agent cannot approve its own pull
# request, so a blanket requirement would block the automated completion path
# forever. That reasoning holds for code. It does not hold for the areas below,
# where the cost of a silent mistake is a compliance problem, a broken gate, or
# a deploy that stops happening.

# Legally load-bearing, machine-parsed, or both.
/docs/                      @alxjrvs
/LLM_STATEMENT.md           @alxjrvs
/SECURITY.md                @alxjrvs

# The gate and the deploy. A change here can turn every other check decorative.
/.github/                   @alxjrvs

# The map every contributor and agent reads before acting.
/CLAUDE.md                  @alxjrvs
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @alxjrvs
